  "caption_groups": [
    {
      "start": 0.852083,
      "end": 3.1437910000000002,
      "text": "Beavers live in freshwater ecosystems such"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.156791,
      "end": 5.760958,
      "text": "as rivers, streams, lakes and ponds across"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.787,
      "end": 6.763583,
      "text": "various regions."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.488083,
      "end": 10.363083,
      "text": "In Europe, beavers were reduced to"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.389125,
      "end": 12.693832999999998,
      "text": "fragmented populations, with combined"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.706833,
      "end": 14.764165999999998,
      "text": "population numbers being estimated at"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.777166,
      "end": 15.896957999999998,
      "text": "various locations."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.212083,
      "end": 19.386582,
      "text": "These estimated groups survived in places"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.399583,
      "end": 20.428248999999997,
      "text": "like the Rhône of France,"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.558457999999998,
      "end": 21.67825,
      "text": "the Elbe in Germany,"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.8475,
      "end": 22.915249,
      "text": "and southern Norway."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.256083,
      "end": 26.495708,
      "text": "Additional survivors remained near the Neman"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.521708,
      "end": 28.592041,
      "text": "river and Dnieper Basin in Belarus,"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.8915,
      "end": 30.896708,
      "text": "along with the Voronezh river in Russia."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.212083,
      "end": 34.607916,
      "text": "The concept became popular in conservation,"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.894375,
      "end": 36.222541,
      "text": "and was deployed in a range of"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.248541,
      "end": 38.488124,
      "text": "contexts by wildlife protection groups."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.832083,
      "end": 41.928458,
      "text": "This framework was mobilized to engender"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.954499999999996,
      "end": 43.282624,
      "text": "support for conservation,"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.63416599999999,
      "end": 45.50916599999999,
      "text": "especially where human activities had"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.535208,
      "end": 48.048249,
      "text": "damaged natural ecosystems significantly."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.396083,
      "end": 51.531499,
      "text": "Such conservation strategies were applied"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.544540999999995,
      "end": 53.445583,
      "text": "especially where human activities had"
    },
    {
      "start": 53.471624999999996,
      "end": 55.867458,
      "text": "damaged ecosystems, such as by removing"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.880458,
      "end": 57.026332,
      "text": "keystone predators."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.360082999999996,
      "end": 60.768957,
      "text": "In addition, wolves often kept animals from"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.794999999999995,
      "end": 62.331457,
      "text": "grazing in riparian areas,"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.617915999999994,
      "end": 64.440833,
      "text": "which protected beavers from having their"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.453833,
      "end": 66.09445799999999,
      "text": "food sources encroached upon."
    }
  ],
